			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				77,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Grove): Add Mermaid diagram for five-layer architecture\n\nInsert a Mermaid sequence diagram into `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` visualizing the Grove native extension host structure. The diagram details the five distinct layers: HOST (lifecycle management), WASM (WASMtime runtime and memory), TRANSPORT (gRPC/IPC/WASM strategies), API (VSCode.rs surface), and PROTOCOL (Spine connection).\n\nIt also illustrates the communication flow between the Protocol layer and the Mountain gRPC server, complementing the existing text-based architectural overview.",
			"SHA": "e1a0b044e1a5b2b23a43b0a0cf981ed65d79d5f0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:23:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				77,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Grove): Add comprehensive architecture documentation\n\nCreate Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md to provide a detailed technical overview of the Grove native Rust/WASM extension host. The document covers the five-layer architecture (Host, WASM, Transport, API, Protocol), transport strategies (gRPC, IPC, WASM), WASMtime runtime sandboxing properties, and the VS Code API surface subset supported.\n\nThe documentation maps key source modules, explains the extension lifecycle from discovery to deactivation, and details the Cargo feature gates controlling build configurations. This aligns Grove's documentation standards with other Land elements like Common and Mountain, clarifying its role as a sandboxed alternative to the Cocoon Node.js extension host.",
			"SHA": "00914e7e41911b9c42ef76a5313554de8099f9d3"
		},
		{
